 Yes, if someone is using your copyrighted image without your permission, you may have a case for copyright infringement. To sue for copyright infringement, you must be able to prove the following elements:

1. You are the copyright owner or have been authorized to enforce the copyright;
2. The defendant has copied your copyrighted work;
3. The copying constitutes infringement by using the work without permission in a way that violates one or more of the exclusive rights granted to the copyright owner under the Copyright Act.

It's important to note that suing for copyright infringement can be a complex and time-consuming process. You may want to consider contacting an intellectual property attorney for advice before taking legal action. Additionally, there are alternatives to suing, such as sending a cease and desist letter, that may be less costly and time-consuming.
